ath-academy-id "q-118782" :question/problem "Which of the following are second-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $9x{y}^{''}+8{y}^{'}=4$\n- **II.** $\\sqrt{{y}^{''}+x}=3y$\n- **III.** ${y}^{‴}+{x}^{2}{y}^{''}=3$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of second-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation II is also a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b78f5f8-eebd-57fd-8d9c-03ba838f7aef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422279} {:answer/id #uuid "4c109920-c2c8-5c61-8b61-0f78d91253a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b78f5f8-eebd-57fd-8d9c-03ba838f7aef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422279} :answer-field/id #uuid "f370d4f5-a457-5b28-ac9a-80af2dd4a8a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ef4fc5-634b-5120-a4df-e7cd35583cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422281} {:answer/id #uuid "5957af20-d016-564c-98a5-0dad4377e784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer