he highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "c834636a-bbd4-5759-b671-beb2e4da2abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f8bc9f-67ba-586b-b99e-1e38a930e19b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "df851142-894b-5bfb-8ece-98c5eb3b201e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408171} {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d9436b-ef55-5798-a20b-5e6bc9ca9430" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "1bb8cc3c-94ce-5d96-9edb-479fa67563b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408174} {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176} :answer-field/id #uuid "495b552a-fc87-5ee2-b05d-892960260624" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408175}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20db6c27-e8a9-50d0-bb54-61baf97c40e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96676" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3{y}^{''}+2x{y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$\n- **II.** $5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$\n- **III.** $\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation II is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\n- Equation III is also a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef08266-c8b5-5d86-ba6c-38cec94b0b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} :answer-field/id #uuid "34bc34b4-9e03-56ed-af57-5921ddebb2d3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} {:answer/id #uuid "5090af3c-f638-5321-a137-c61895760b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b81d3a8-27c9-5a56-9c75-a52909222499" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7601c375-892a-5f42-948b-dc68c11393c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422295} {:answer/id #uuid "4fae8008-076c-53ed-87cb-e76c044c94bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true"