erivative in this equation is ${y}^{′},$ so this is a first-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53060f3c-37ba-5269-99e6-437127908eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358467} {:answer/id #uuid "779e8577-9f6e-5fa7-924b-e37a99f1b28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358783} {:answer/id #uuid "8704391c-698c-5b53-8da1-2de5b7777a0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358934} {:answer/id #uuid "aab69c40-d839-5b4b-94d1-7d9e857ba71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359221} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d51d2e-5951-5e07-ab5d-d620a48d77f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aab69c40-d839-5b4b-94d1-7d9e857ba71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359221} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9cba9eb-cca7-50bc-8d85-f1b4fa7b959a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e716837-33b2-54de-96d4-f505ade9217f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96662" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+5{y}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3{y}^{5}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}},$ which has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360692 :question/ans